//! The `vector-effect` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property suppresses
//! specific [transformation
//! effects](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Reference/Attribute/transform) in SVG,
//! thus permitting effects like a road on a map staying the same width no matter how the map is
//! zoomed, or allowing a diagram key to retain its position and size regardless of other transforms.
//! It can only be used with SVG elements that accept the `vector-effect` attribute. When used, the
//! CSS value overrides any values of the element's `vector-effect` attribute.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: none | non-scaling-stroke | non-scaling-size | non-rotation | fixed-position
//!
//! Specification: https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/coords.html#VectorEffectProperty
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/vector-effect
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

